From f660d1f93bf105cea21d5f5dc07e24674102f495 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 14:29:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 144/638] content: drain AROS browser tasks before unload
 [chromium] [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-headless-bringup

AI_STATUS: done

ROOT_CAUSE: ThreadPoolInstance::Shutdown intentionally permits CONTINUE_ON_SHUTDOWN workers and pooled single-thread runners to survive. Once collect-aros restored pthread's EXIT hook, AROS correctly refused to unload headless_shell while artifact 50 still showed twelve pool tasks plus MemoryInfra waiting.

FIX_REASON: After every browser subsystem has stopped posting work, join all ThreadPool groups and pooled single-thread runners, then stop the leaky MemoryInfra thread through the final-shutdown API. This supplies the process-wide task termination that AROS cannot inherit from a host process boundary.

SCOPE: Final BrowserMainLoop teardown on AROS only; normal shutdown semantics on other platforms are unchanged.

VALIDATION: browser_main_loop.o and the new MemoryDumpManager API compiled successfully in the 166/166 touched-target build; OPAL artifact 50 maps each targeted task to the drained owners.

RISK: medium; JoinForTesting is intentionally final and forbids later task posting, so it is placed after PostDestroyThreads and guarded to AROS.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
---
 content/browser/browser_main_loop.cc | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/content/browser/browser_main_loop.cc b/content/browser/browser_main_loop.cc
index e9608c7322..40087ce5a3 100644
--- a/content/browser/browser_main_loop.cc
+++ b/content/browser/browser_main_loop.cc
@@ -1288,6 +1288,20 @@ void BrowserMainLoop::ShutdownThreadsAndCleanUp() {
     TRACE_EVENT0("shutdown", "BrowserMainLoop::Subsystem:PostDestroyThreads");
     parts_->PostDestroyThreads();
   }
+
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_AROS)
+  // AROS unloads an executable's code as soon as its main task returns.
+  // Shutdown() intentionally permits CONTINUE_ON_SHUTDOWN workers to remain
+  // alive, so join the pool after every browser subsystem has stopped posting
+  // work. This also drains its single-thread task runners before pthread's
+  // process-exit hook verifies that no task can execute unloaded code.
+  LOG(INFO) << "[Chromium:shutdown] joining AROS ThreadPool workers";
+  base::ThreadPoolInstance::Get()->JoinForTesting();
+  LOG(INFO) << "[Chromium:shutdown] AROS ThreadPool workers joined";
+  LOG(INFO) << "[Chromium:shutdown] stopping AROS MemoryInfra thread";
+  base::trace_event::MemoryDumpManager::GetInstance()->ShutdownForProcessExit();
+  LOG(INFO) << "[Chromium:shutdown] AROS MemoryInfra thread stopped";
+#endif
 }
 
 media::AudioManager* BrowserMainLoop::audio_manager() const {
